From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The video recorder's picture, drawn again at a size of its own

Patch 0053 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-09, of the program's new MP4 recorder: "choose the output resolution", and "use
4K for the output of the recording while still allowing me to play it at my resolution".

Two hooks beside the draw hook (rt64_render_hooks): a size hook, asked once per presented frame
with the window's size, and a picture hook. When the size hook answers with a size, the present
draws the VI pass a second time into a B8G8R8A8_UNORM target of that size (pictureTexture, kept
while the size holds and given back after 600 presents without a picture), with no panel inset and
nothing drawn over it, moves it to COPY_SOURCE and hands it to the picture hook, then sets the swap
chain's framebuffer back for the draw hook. The picture is the window's: the same crop, gamma and
fit, from the game's own render target, so it may be larger than the window.

VIRenderer::RenderParams gains targetWidth and targetHeight (0 is the swap chain, as before), and
getViewportAndScissor a second form that takes a named target size in place of the swap chain's;
the first form forwards to it. Declared as a second form, and the hooks' code placed beside the
other hooks rather than at the end of the file, so that no hunk touches a file's last line: those
lines have no line ending, and git's line ending conversion of the series would break such a hunk.

diff --git a/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.h b/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.h
--- a/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.h
+++ b/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.h
@@ -16,4 +16,17 @@ namespace RT64 {
     RenderHookDeinit *GetRenderHookDeinit();
 
     void SetRenderHooks(RenderHookInit *init, RenderHookDraw *draw, RenderHookDeinit *deinit);
+
+    // THE GAME'S PICTURE AT A SIZE OF THE PROGRAM'S CHOOSING (patch 0053, OoT: Recompiled, for its
+    // video recorder). Once per presented frame that has a picture, the present asks the size hook
+    // whether a picture is wanted, telling it the window's size. When it answers yes, with a size,
+    // the present draws the VI pass a second time into a B8G8R8A8_UNORM target of that size (the
+    // same crop, gamma and fit as the window gets, with no panel inset and nothing drawn over it)
+    // and hands that target to the picture hook in COPY_SOURCE, where it must be left. The size
+    // may be larger than the window: the picture is drawn from the game's own render target.
+    using RenderHookPictureSize = bool(uint32_t windowWidth, uint32_t windowHeight, uint32_t *width, uint32_t *height);
+    using RenderHookPicture = void(RenderCommandList *list, RenderTexture *picture, uint32_t width, uint32_t height);
+    RenderHookPictureSize *GetRenderHookPictureSize();
+    RenderHookPicture *GetRenderHookPicture();
+    void SetRenderHookPicture(RenderHookPictureSize *size, RenderHookPicture *picture);
 };
diff --git a/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.cpp b/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.cpp
--- a/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.cpp
+++ b/src/rhi/rt64_render_hooks.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,23 @@ namespace RT64 {
     static RenderHookDraw *draw = nullptr;
     static RenderHookDeinit *deinit = nullptr;
 
+    // Patch 0053.
+    static RenderHookPictureSize *pictureSize = nullptr;
+    static RenderHookPicture *picture = nullptr;
+
+    RenderHookPictureSize *GetRenderHookPictureSize() {
+        return pictureSize;
+    }
+
+    RenderHookPicture *GetRenderHookPicture() {
+        return picture;
+    }
+
+    void SetRenderHookPicture(RenderHookPictureSize *pictureSize_, RenderHookPicture *picture_) {
+        pictureSize = pictureSize_;
+        picture = picture_;
+    }
+
     RenderHookInit *GetRenderHookInit() {
         return init;
     }
